--- body ---
## Scope

Move the current local MiniLM configuration out of its constructor chain into
one versioned registry file. Do not add a selector, alternate entry, daemon or
behavior change.

## Exit criteria

- [x] A characterization test freezes current query and passage vectors, dimension
  and vector key before the extraction.
- [x] The singleton entry carries the incumbent model, revision, graph/dtype,
  pooling, normalization, templates, window and dimension explicitly.
- [x] The characterization stays green after the extraction.

## Where the work lives

The fork, branch `t0489-minilm-singleton-entry`, based on the reviewed upstream
SHA `b05ed69a88e3a0c1ef874f57f97a0e11ddf7ec3c` (v1.12.0). The embedder seam was
untouched on `conductor-integration`, so no rebasing onto ticket 0568's work was
needed: `src/features/search/embeddings.ts` is identical at both refs.

| commit | what |
|---|---|
| `8d2893cf819d9b521ce6023645b6c8d3d76d3947` | `src/features/search/embedder-registry.ts`, the characterization test and its frozen fixture, with the chain still untouched |
| `4b2e32edd56b3943e7b332b54d14191fffa0e1df` | `embeddings.ts` reads model, pooling and normalization from the entry |
| `6b5ac4cbbb0114acc96e51ef112a55d245fa8661` | the fixture's capture stamp, which had been local wall-clock wearing a `Z` and postdated its own commit |

## What the entry declares

`INCUMBENT_LOCAL_ENTRY`, id `minilm-l6-v2`: model `Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`,
revision `main` (which resolved to `751bff37182d3f1213fa05d7196b954e230abad9` on
2026-09-02), device `cpu`, dtype `fp32`, graph `onnx/model.onnx`, pooling `mean`,
normalize `true`, templates empty on both sides, window 256 tokens, dimension
384. Every value carries the source it was read from; pooling comes from
`1_Pooling/config.json` on `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`, which the
Xenova ONNX mirror does not publish.

Three fields are authoritative today (`APPLIED_FIELDS`: model, pooling,
normalize). Seven are declared and unread (`DECLARED_ONLY_FIELDS`). Two describe
the record rather than the embedder (`ENTRY_METADATA_FIELDS`: id, sources). The
test asserts those three lists partition the record's keys, so a field belonging
to none of them, or to two, fails the suite and the gap cannot go quiet. Pinning the
revision or the dtype was considered and rejected for this stage: under Node the
runtime resolves fp32, but on the wasm device its default is q8, so writing fp32
here would move the vectors on an install class this branch cannot test.

## Finding: the declared window is not the window in force

The model card declares a 256-token window
(`sentence_bert_config.json max_seq_length`). The feature-extraction pipeline
truncates at the tokenizer's own `model_max_length`, which
`tokenizer_config.json` sets to 512. Measured: a 660-token passage is cut to 512.
The fixture freezes that passage's vector, so whichever way 0490 resolves the
disagreement, the change is visible rather than silent.
